            "review_title": "Review at Kemuri Donburi",
            "review_text": "Ina D\nManila, Philippines184 contributions\n0\nA Gem in the City\nMay 2019 • Family\nWe just chanced upon the place as we were looking around before we went to the Opera House. The place is nothing fancy. Just a few tables outside and an open air counter. Appearances were deceiving! They serve unlimited tea which is SO REFRESHING. \nWhen the food arrived and we dug in, the first bite was HEAVEN!!! We ordered the deep fried chicken and the grilled chicken donburi. All dishes were served with kimchi and egg and both dishes were REALLY good!!!! The fried chicken was so yummy and flaky and the grilled chicken was marinated well and both were cooked to perfection. The way they mixed the rice, with the meat, seasonings and garnishing, it was so well done that even our nine year old who is a picky eater finished his bowl. \nUnfortunately, we were not able to visit the place again but given the chance to go back to Ho Chi Minh, this would definitely be our first meal there as we miss already the food!!!!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten June 6, 2019\nSusan832014\nThank so much Ina D for your comment and hope we can meet in another time when you come to Ho Chi Minh.\nWritten June 30, 2019\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
